WEBVTT

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.590
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.590
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.590
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.210 --> 00:02:02.310
Chapter VI

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:10.510
On December 7th, the Imperial Fleet belatedly realized the idiocy of splitting their fleets...

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:14.840
...and rejoined with the detached units that were pursuing the back-turn advancement.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.610
I don't understand.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.200
My units were executing the back-turn
advancement in accordance with our initial plan.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:28.760
We were forced to suspend
it in the midst of our operation.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.390
<b>Vice Admiral Kaltenborn</b>

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.650
<b>Admiral Schreiter</b>

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.980
To turn back without entering the battle...

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.100
<b>Vice Admiral Keit</b>

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.480
...is the utmost disgrace for a warrior.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.000
I demand a convincing explanation.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.890
Despite losing the
Muckenberger Fleet...

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:44.100
...the Imperial Fleet still held the size
advantage and its morale remained high.

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:50.480
On the other hand, the Alliance also regrouped their forces and was preparing for the renewal of hostilities.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.140
But the internal conflict in the
Alliance Command Headquarters...

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.120
...was becoming even
more heated and intense.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.320
Though present in the meeting,
Cope did not even try to speak out...

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.170
...and Ashbey was also ignoring his
comrades who questioned his orders.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:10.040
But Cope wasn't the only one who
was angered by Ashbey's attitude.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.730
So you think everything
in the palm of your hand ?

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:16.810
Do you actually think that wars are
fought by just the Chief Commander ?

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:20.340
Why don't you try and defeat
the Imperial Fleet all by yourself ?

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.280
Upset after consecutive hard battles,
Warwick did not hold back his opinions.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.300
The members of the 730 Mafia
were talented as military commanders...

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.690
...and were not at all deficient
as human beings either.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.720
And some could be
described as noble-minded.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:42.760
But the lifetime of the group as a whole might have been nearing its end, though no one seemed to know.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.400
At the 2nd Battle of
Tiamat, these commanders...

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:51.020
...who had previously fought
their battles together as friends...

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:54.890
...pursued their own interests and were at loggerheads with each other more than usual.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:59.600
To begin with, this was an error in your personnel decisions.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:05.020
You placed me in the rear-line and
put an unmotivated Bertini in the front.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:08.900
Because of that, Cope and Warwick had
to fight in unnecessarily harsh conditions.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:16.450
It was only as a matter of consequence that you didn't face their detached fleet.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:19.760
The rear-line defense itself wasn't unimportant or unnecessary.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:24.600
But that doesn't change the fact that my fleet was left empty-handed.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.200
Don't you think that was a waste ?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.000
This is my victory
battle, you know {i.e. according to his jinx} ?

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:32.860
I got it.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.730
Next time, I'll leave you in
charge of the front line.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:40.140
By the time both sides moved
again after receiving supplies...

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.320
...it was already December 8th.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.140
<b>4th Fleet Flagship - Brigitte</b>

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:46.040
First, the Alliance 4th Fleet began to advance.

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:49.550
March Jasper's victory
jinx didn't disappoint.

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:53.140
In just 15 minutes of battle...

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:57.710
...Jasper succeeded in cleanly cutting
open the Imperial Fleet's dense formation.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.940
According to the Alliance
Fleet's official records...

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.000
...it was described as "like cutting
a piece of cheese with a knife."

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:06.800
What are you all doing ?

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.700
Execute a flanking attack on the
advancing rebel forces from both sides !

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.300
All ships, turn 90 degrees !

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.900
<b>Keit Fleet Flagship - Embla</b>

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:20.930
Now, charge !

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:26.250
Incoming attack !
It's from a different fleet !

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.100
What ?

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.710
Battleship Merwin was sunk.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:35.680
Sub-commander Rear Admiral
Meinrich has been killed !

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.610
You rebels,
I won't forgive you !

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.940
Come about again
and counter-attack !

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:56.410
The enemy fleet is retreating !

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.320
Looks like we can
win, doesn't it ?

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:03.040
The problem is whether or
not we can continue to win.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.700
How is the battle going ?

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.490
Are we winning or losing ?

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.660
I don't know.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.920
Just don't waste your ammo !

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.530
We've just been re-supplied.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.190
Battleship Skuld
has been destroyed.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.020
Commander, I think our
ship should withdraw.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:21.950
It's dangerous.

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:22.730
Idiot !

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:23.950
I can't retreat !

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.220
But since the sub-commander has been killed, if something were to happen to the you...

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.120
...our fleet would be in disarray !

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:33.940
At this stage, it's more preferable to
bear a temporary disgrace than to...

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.370
Direct hits, incoming !

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:37.320
What ?

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:46.740
Vice Admiral Keit did not die, but was
critically injured and lost consciousness.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.590
As the chief staff
officer feared...

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:52.600
...the Imperial fleet in this area became
disorganized and dispersed while retreating.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:57.510
If the Alliance Fleet had
deployed a an aggressive pursuit...

00:06:57.510 --> 00:07:00.820
...it would have immediately changed
the course of the battle as a whole.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:06.080
But the damage and fatigue to
Warwick's fleet was also considerable.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:10.110
We'll withdraw to the
fleet line for a while.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:10.790
Get us some distance.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:15.730
The cooperative effort between Jasper and Warwick brought tremendous results in this area of the battle.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:21.490
But on the whole the Imperial and Alliance Fleets continuously repeated advancement and withdrawal...

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:25.490
...and between December 8th and 9th, the battle was completely in stasis.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:28.220
It was hard to tell which
side held the advantage.

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:32.740
In any case, the Imperial Fleet will stick
to their back-turn advancement plan.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:35.440
Consider it an
unchangeable fact.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:40.760
To counter this, we must have a separate fleet following the enemy movement...

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:46.390
...and at an optimal point,
we'll hit them from their flank.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:50.590
We'll assemble this detached unit from the ships from each fleet...

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:52.590
...and I will directly command
the unit for the attack.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:59.680
So Fang, I want you take
3,000 ships from your 8th Fleet...

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.300
...and transfer them to the
command of General Headquarters.

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:06.090
I can't.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:07.680
What ?

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.190
Why ?

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:10.730
Why can't you ?

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:14.690
Please don't ask what
you already know.

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:19.900
If I take 3,000 ships from my fleet,
I can't maintain the battlelines in this area.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:24.250
If I don't have 3,000 ships, all
of our fleets will be annihilated.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:27.430
If that happens, are you going
to take responsibility for it ?!

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:33.900
Regardless of whether or not I'll take responsibility I'd like to know why you're making such a demand.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.870
Don't you get it
without an explanation ?

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:38.910
How long have we
been fighting together ?

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:46.400
After a short but fierce confrontation,
Fang agreed to give him 3,000 ships.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:53.040
As Ashbey predicted, the Imperial Fleet
sought to break out of the stalemate....

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.780
...by reverting back to the initial plan of a back-turn advancement.

00:08:56.690 --> 00:09:00.120
By attempting to move all fleets in a clockwise, back-turn advancement...

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:04.420
...they sought to trap the Alliance fleets in the half-enveloping formation.

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:13.250
But having foreseen this movement, the Alliance fleets followed their movement.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:21.200
It looked like two dragons trying to go after each other's tail, moving round and round.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:29.210
In this manner, the battle entered December
10th, and the stalemate conditions continued.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:35.740
Unable to bear the stringency
of this situation...

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:40.440
...the Imperial Kaltenborn Fleet
turned to a rush attack.

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:40.590
<b>Kaltenborn Fleet Flagship - Dagda</b>

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:41.940
Charge !

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:49.640
With incredible speed and firepower, the Kaltenborn Fleet began attacking the Alliance fleets.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:56.180
Commander, the Kaltenborn Fleet has moved into brilliant assault formation.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.470
How thoughtless....

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:00.000
We'll go to their aid, hurry !

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:01.270
Huh ?

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:07.310
The Imperial Fleet's decisive attack was a tragic waste of courage and human lives.

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:14.820
The Kaltenborn Fleet withstood the counterattack and took control of the F4 Space Area...

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:17.490
...but there, they reached
the limit of their advance.

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:22.020
Jasper did not let that one-second window of opportunity escape him.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:23.550
All ships, come about and attack !

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:28.480
That swiftness of movement
impressed both allies and enemies.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.850
Good job, Jasper.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:35.700
Brilliant...

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:51.310
Direct hits, incoming !

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:04.040
As I thought,
we couldn't make it in time.

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.480
We'll rescue our allies, hurry !

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:11.360
Steiermark divided his fleet
into small units of 40 ships...

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:15.590
...and created a highly organic
system of support and withdrawal.

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:19.140
In the end, it seemed that he would
succeed in withdrawing all his fleets...

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:21.040
...essentially unscathed
from the Alliance attack.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:26.490
But at that point, Fang Tchew-ling
launched a flanking attack.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.500
<b>8th Fleet Flagship - Gora-daileng</b>

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:31.710
Fire.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:37.320
Flanked, the Imperial Fleet was
exposed to a broadside assault.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:43.700
Moreover, suffering from repeated
attacks by high-speed assault cruisers...

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:47.000
...the Imperial Fleet lost
2,000 ships before withdrawing.

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:54.140
The members
of the 730 Mafia...

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:59.310
...proved once again that they were highly
talented and capable fleet commanders.

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:05.640
But at 16:40, the situation
changed dramatically.

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:10.790
The Imperial fleets, albeit imperfectly,
completed their back-turn advancement...

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:15.340
...and fiercely started attacking the rear
of the 5th and 8th Fleets of the Alliance Fleet.

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:18.040
The assault was more
relentless than ever.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.640
Don't let them through !

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.280
If we let them, our
battle lines will collapse.

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:33.100
No, they're already
starting to collapse.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:38.550
The present size comparison is 1 to 2, to our disadvantage.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:44.090
In the face of pressure from an enemy
twice our size, small tactics are of no use.

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:51.480
The 4th Fleet came to their rescue, and flanked the Imperial Fleet...

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:55.030
...but was counter-attacked
with firepower ten times larger.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:02.190
What's Bruce doing ?

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:04.690
Ashbey, how long are you
going to make us wait ?

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:08.140
Well, whether Ashbey or
Death arrives here first...

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:10.900
...the race is an
interesting one to watch.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:16.710
All the commanders in the Alliance fleet were almost at their psychological breaking point.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:18.740
If they don't launch
a large-scale attack...

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:21.490
...the Imperial Fleet will complete
its back-turn advancement...

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:25.090
...and the Alliance fleet will even lose their route of withdrawal back home.

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:26.700
Because they knew that,
they became anxious.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.490
It's our ally, the Chief Commander's fleet !

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:42.900
At 18:10, the situation
changed again dramatically.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.760
The Imperial fleets were attacked
from both front and rear.

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:51.250
Ashbey's choice of attack
direction was indeed godlike.

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:57.140
He swiftly moved in to shave off the left-side of the Imperial Fleet and then changed direction midway...

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:02.840
...to cut through diagonally, collapsing the Imperial fleet into utter disarray.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:07.820
The enemy fleets
are collapsing !

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:11.690
How's that ?

00:14:19.950 --> 00:14:21.420
What happened to Bertini ?

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:25.140
He has died.

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:31.800
There's just been a report from interim
commander, Admiral Copperfield.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:39.020
I see.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:42.350
Bertini got the promotion to
Fleet Admiral faster than I.

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:49.480
Withdraw the 9th Fleet for the
time being and let them regroup.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:53.830
At the death of Bertini, the
Alliance Fleet was in tears.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:57.760
But the tears in the Imperial Fleet
were well over three times greater.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:03.510
Inside the large-scale trap that
Bruce Ashbey industriously built...

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:06.980
...the Imperial fleets winced and writhed like wounded prey.

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:10.120
At that point, there was no system or order...

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:11.950
...all they could do was run away from the enemy's hands.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:20.810
The time of the decisive end to this battle was said to have been at about 18:50 on December 11th.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:19.310
<b>Schreiter Fleet Flagship - Bergelmir</b>

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.740
In a battle of only
about 40 minutes...

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:26.620
...the Imperial Fleet suffered
the loss of about 60 admirals.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:30.140
Among them were Admiral Schreiter...

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:32.550
...Admiral Kosel, and other
battle-experienced commanders.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:35.250
<b>Kosel Fleet Flagship - Diarium</b>

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:37.360
It is said that it took
the Imperial Fleet a decade...

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:41.140
...to recover from the losses
incurred in those 40 minutes.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:52.340
The fleet that sustained its systematic resistance
and withdrawal support efforts until the last moment...

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:57.140
...was the Steiermark
Fleet, but at 18:52...

00:15:57.140 --> 00:16:00.910
...it finally relinquished the idea of
sustaining the battle and started retreating.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:07.390
Shortly afterwards, Ashbey's
flagship, the Hard-luck...

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:09.240
...started to advance past
the main battlefield...

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:13.430
...protected by three
cruisers and six destroyers.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:18.480
Reacting to the sporadic attacks
from isolated enemy ships...

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:21.340
...the escorts took a slight
distance from the flagship.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:26.740
Truly, it was at that brief moment:
fate that took the form of a stray bullet...

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:30.370
...tearing into the Hard-luck's
midsection, right-bottom part.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:42.500
Commander...

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:57.790
Battles these days...have
become ill-natured, like women.

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:08.440
Hey, Rosas, hate to trouble you, but call the doctor right away.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:14.310
If I don't close up this wound, everyone will find out that I'm evil-hearted.

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:14.760
Doctor !

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:15.520
Doctor !

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:34.140
The naval surgeon
arrived immediately...

00:17:34.140 --> 00:17:38.620
...but all he could do was confirm the time of Ashbey's death.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:41.990
On December 11th, 19:09.

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:45.860
The cause of death was shock and hemorrhaging from lacerations around the stomach area.

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:53.910
Did we win ?

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:56.740
They ran away,
and we're still here.

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:59.580
Generally speaking, we call
that a victory, don't we ?

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:03.250
At that moment,
another report came in...

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:09.550
...and the members of the 730 Mafia
learned that their leader was lost forever.

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:16.490
Despite achieving decisive
victory in this battle...

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:21.400
...the Alliance Fleet returned home in grave and bitter silence without celebratory champagne.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:26.170
After the New Year, on January 4th, an elaborate national commemoration was carried out...

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:28.780
...and Ashbey was given the
title of Fleet Admiral.

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:31.480
If he had been alive, he would have been 36 years old...

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:34.590
...but he was still the youngest Fleet Admiral in the history of the Alliance Fleet.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:39.140
Even the heroes of Dagon,
Limpao and Yusuf Tparl...

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:42.480
...did not receive the title of Fleet Admiral until they were 40 years of age.

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:50.980
The youngest Fleet Admiral in
the history of the Alliance Fleet....

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:54.140
In order to make
Ashbey's fame eternal...

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:57.040
...the top officials in the military
engaged in political maneuvers.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:03.140
Bertini, who also died at Tiamat,
was kept at Admiral upon his death...

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:08.720
...and wasn't given the title of Fleet
Admiral until six years after his death.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:14.400
Preferential treatment like this contributed to heightening Ashbey's fame...

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:16.640
...and, at the same time, resulted in antipathy in some corners.

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:26.040
Thank you very much
for your valuable time.

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:27.690
Don't mention it.

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:30.250
I've mostly talked about things
I'd already written in my memoir.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:32.710
There weren't any new
discoveries, were there ?

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:37.590
No.  But to hear the
story directly from you...

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:38.740
Yes, you're right.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:42.800
If you want to hear more stories
like this, feel free to come again.

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:44.270
Thank you.

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:45.330
I'll see you again.

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:45.960
Yes.

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:56.540
Thank you for your trouble.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.320
Are you researching into
the life of Bruce Ashbey ?

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.130
Y...yes, something like that.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:05.390
He was a friend of
Admiral Rosas, wasn't he ?

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:08.940
Bruce Ashbey, my
grandfather's friend ?

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:10.270
Give me a break.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.870
That man stole my
grandfather's accomplishments.

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:14.660
Huh ?

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:22.310
There are many kinds of thieves - those who steal nations, those who steal others' wives.

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:26.380
And the worst among them are those who steal other people's accomplishments.

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:28.100
Don't you agree ?

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:30.600
I agree, as a
general opinion.

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:35.880
Admiral Ashbey isn't here
to refute your denouncement.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:41.360
As far as I'm concerned, I'd like to
collect small voices from all quarters...

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:46.550
You have a tendency
to talk so insincerely.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:47.930
I'm sorry.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:51.140
You don't have to apologize.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:53.480
I'm the one who's
saying terrible things.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:55.270
You only have to laugh
and not take me seriously.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:21:01.390
Your brain cells will explode if you listen
intently to all these irresponsible opinions.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:04.050
I'll be careful.

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:07.490
You're strange.

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:12.540
And are there any 
grounds for your opinion ?

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:13.510
I don't know.

00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:14.830
It's your job, isn't it ?

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.430
Why don't you find
it out yourself, Mr. MP ?

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.250
I wish she called me a
"private detective" at least.

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:38.210
If there is a possibility of premeditated
murder in Ashbey's death, where is it ?

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:42.220
Does it mean that the Imperial Fleet knew the exact position of the Flagship Hard-luck ?

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:47.030
In other words, the information of the 
Alliance Fleet was leaked to the enemy.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:48.580
Someone leaked the
information intentionally.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:50.100
Who did it ?

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:52.740
Inside the Alliance...

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:56.470
...there was worry and distrust directed toward Ashbey and the 730 Mafia.

00:21:57.330 --> 00:22:02.070
Much like how Rudolf von Goldenbaum
usurped the Galactic Empire previously...

00:22:02.070 --> 00:22:05.540
...there were worries that the 730 Mafia would become a political clique...

00:22:05.540 --> 00:22:08.150
...and create a militaristic autocracy with their military force...

00:22:08.150 --> 00:22:11.490
...and unquestionable popularity
among the masses as their backbone.

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:17.190
But on the other hand, it was also troublesome if the Alliance lost the 2nd Battle of Tiamat.

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:20.140
For this dilemma
to be resolved...

00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:23.760
...the Alliance Fleet should defeat the
Empire while Ashbey dies in the battle.

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:26.820
And the outcome turned
out to be ideal, but...

00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:33.290
Sorry to disturb your personal ivory tower, but there's a little news.

00:22:33.680 --> 00:22:34.950
What happened ?

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:36.280
Did someone die ?

00:22:36.760 --> 00:22:38.920
Admiral Rosas passed away.

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:40.570
What ?

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:43.790
And it wasn't
a natural death.

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:47.470
It could be an accident, suicide,
or even a possible homicide.

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:50.350
This has gotten
a little complicated.

00:22:51.920 --> 00:22:55.790
Yang was shocked at
the unexpected denouement.

00:22:55.790 --> 00:22:58.740
Forty years after the
2nd Battle of Tiamat...

00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:01.200
...the situation was taking
an unforeseeable direction.

00:22:58.830 --> 00:23:03.730
The Death of a Hero

00:22:58.830 --> 00:23:03.730
